      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "dodge_ram_truck_stereotype",
      "label": "Dodge Ram Truck Owner Stereotype",
      "description": "The stereotype that Dodge Ram truck owners are overly proud of their vehicles, often to the point of refusing to be photographed or acknowledging their truck's presence. This is a common trope in car enthusiast culture and internet memes, often used humorously to exaggerate the owner's attachment to their vehicle. The meme relies on this stereotype to create its comedic effect.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_0b8228f4"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_aa38ba2f",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "public_parade_event",
      "label": "Public Parade Event",
      "description": "The background scene of the image, featuring people on horseback and spectators, suggests a public parade or festival. This context is important because it implies a public, possibly chaotic or crowded environment, which contrasts with the owner's apparent desire to avoid being photographed. The meme uses this setting to heighten the humor by juxtaposing the owner's pride with the public nature of the event.",
